add('sources.html','Sources and implementation','Read the original plan, inspect the repository and distinguish working features from the proposed connected system.',head('Follow the idea<br>back to its source.','The source plan leads the content. The public implementation makes its current capabilities visible and keeps future connections clear.')+f'''<section class="section"><div class="wrap split"><div><h2>The original plan</h2><p><em>The Joyful Responsible Abundance Product Engine</em>, Luke Nathan Hayes, 28 September 2026. 21 pages.</p><p>The PDF is published with the author’s approval and preserved without editing. This site adapts its explanation for a public audience.</p><a class="btn" href="sources/JRA-Product-Engine-Plan.pdf">Read the original PDF ↗</a></div><div class="card"><h3>About this edition</h3><p>Public explanation and implementation by Luke Nathan Hayes / Strange But True / Aura of Intelligence, assisted by AI.</p><p>All four concept artworks, including the favicon, were generated for this site. They do not depict tested products, operating facilities or confirmed partners.</p><p><a href="{REPO}/blob/main/IMAGE-PROMPTS.md">View the artwork prompts</a></p></div></div></section><section class="section tint"><div class="wrap"><h2>What works here</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Capability</th><th scope="col">This public edition</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Product planning</th><td>Blank records and nine editable case-study presets, with stable references and saved versions.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Costs and continued use</th><td>Transparent AUD estimates, break-even quantities, return comparisons and receiving-route notes.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Connected work</th><td>Several contributions and product links per record, with terms and source links.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Portable outputs</th><td>Markdown release packs and JSON backups, including version snapshots. Backup import restores a workspace.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">AI handoffs</th><td>Editable task scopes and permission status. An optional read-only browser tool exposes the open record where supported.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Commerce and agents</th><td>Live agents, payments, orders, stock, shared accounts and external publication are future integrations.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="source-line">Workbench records stay in the browser on the device where they are entered. There are no site analytics or form submissions. Web fonts are requested from Google Fonts; normal hosting access logs may still exist. If you explicitly use a browser AI tool, the open record is returned to that tool.</p></div></section><section class="section"><div class="wrap"><h2>Public project references</h2><p>The links below come from the plan’s reference page, with a verified public GAJRA Earth repository added as an entry point. Descriptions explain their role in the plan; they do not claim active integration.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Reference</th><th scope="col">Connection described in the plan</th></tr></thead><tbody>{reference_rows}</tbody></table></div><div style="margin-top:35px">{extra_links}</div></div></section><section class="section green"><div class="wrap prose"><h2>Documents behind the plan</h2><p>The source PDF also names <em>Community Hours and Joyful Responsible Abundance</em>; <em>Do Not Put All Our Eggs in One Basket</em>; the Aura clothing, consumables and business plans; the Aura Undies presentation; <em>Merchandise.xlsx</em>; the Strange but True strategy and business plan; the GAJRA Earth Civic AI Commons business plan; and the mind-behind-the-man source register.</p><p>Those files were not supplied for this website build. They are referenced through the plan and have not been independently checked or republished here.</p><h2>Inspect, learn and adapt.</h2><p>The repository contains the site, page builder, functional workbench and original artwork prompts. Personal and other permitted non-commercial use follows the Strange But True Public Source Licence. Commercial and corporate rights remain reserved to Luke Nathan Hayes.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn" href="{REPO}">Open the repository ↗</a><a class="btn secondary" href="licence.html">Read the licence</a></div></div></section>''')
